1
00:00:08,013 --> 00:00:11,833
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:16,689
I want you to listen to these Ahadith(احاديث) and keep in mind that, Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد) was a king.

3
00:00:16,956 --> 00:00:18,736
He was an a Nabi(نَبِي), and he was a king.

4
00:00:18,942 --> 00:00:27,368
He was busy with establishing a kingdom, with fighting his enemies, with establishing justice, with establishing services for his people.

5
00:00:28,488 --> 00:00:30,369
And then look at! What else he is doing.

6
00:00:30,495 --> 00:00:32,709
Even though, he's doing all of this; look at what else

7
00:00:32,734 --> 00:00:34,535
Rasool Allah ﷺ says he was doing;

8
00:00:34,795 --> 00:00:41,345
أفْضَلَ الصَّوْمِ صَوْمُ اَخِى دَاوُدَ كانَ يَصُومُ يَوْمًا وَيُفْطِرُ يَوْمًا

9
00:00:41,772 --> 00:00:45,000
The best fasting, is the fasting of my brother; Dawood(داؤد).

10
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:50,449
He would fast one day and break the next.

11
00:00:52,162 --> 00:00:53,922
So he would alternate between fasting.

12
00:00:55,102 --> 00:00:57,478
He would alternate between fasting throughout his life.

13
00:00:58,505 --> 00:01:05,078
This is the king; whatever types of food or drink he wants; he can just point and they would approach him.

14
00:01:05,711 --> 00:01:06,738
But he would fast.

15
00:01:08,458 --> 00:01:13,963
And Rasool Allah ﷺ tells us something else about this Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى,

16
00:01:14,017 --> 00:01:15,217
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

17
00:01:15,763 --> 00:01:17,986
ولا يَفِرُّ إذا لاقَى

18
00:01:18,599 --> 00:01:20,893
He would never run away from battle.

19
00:01:21,253 --> 00:01:28,132
If he's in the battlefield; Dawood(داؤد) would never show the enemy his back; brave and strong.

20
00:01:28,638 --> 00:01:31,028
Rasool Allah ﷺ also says about Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد);

21
00:01:31,088 --> 00:01:33,542
أَحَبَّ الصِّيَامِ إلى اللهِ، صِيَامُ دَاوُدَ،

22
00:01:33,782 --> 00:01:36,062
وَأَحَبَّ الصَّلَاةِ إلى اللهِ، صَلَاةُ دَاوُدَ،

23
00:01:36,268 --> 00:01:40,095
كانَ يَنَامُ نِصْفَهُ، ويقومُ ثُلُثَهُ، وَيَنَامُ سُدُسَهُ،

24
00:01:40,248 --> 00:01:42,068
وَكانَ يَصُومُ يَوْمًا، وَيُفْطِرُ يَوْمًا

25
00:01:42,338 --> 00:01:48,887
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; The best fasting is the fasting of Dawood(داؤد); and the best prayers are the prayers of Dawood(داؤد).

26
00:01:49,347 --> 00:01:57,917
He used to sleep the first half of the night; and then he would wake up and pray for one third of the night;

27
00:01:58,224 --> 00:02:01,325
 and then he would sleep for the remaining one sixth of the night.

28
00:02:01,492 --> 00:02:04,125
So every night, he would pray one third of the night.

29
00:02:05,365 --> 00:02:06,270
He had time for Ibadah(عبادة).

30
00:02:06,290 --> 00:02:07,876
You have to find time for Ibadah(عبادة).

31
00:02:08,276 --> 00:02:14,725
You might say; well, he's busy, he's king, he's is busy with running the affairs of his kingdom, how could he find time for this Ibadah(عبادة).

32
00:02:15,138 --> 00:02:28,052
We need to understand that we cannot be good in whatever we're doing, and be successful in applying the law of Allah and making Da'wah(دعوة);

33
00:02:28,612 --> 00:02:35,558
If we are not having these moments of deep worship with Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

34
00:02:36,271 --> 00:02:41,379
In the depth of the night, and the Dhikr(ذكر), and the fasting are important for any Muslim

35
00:02:41,412 --> 00:02:45,747
who's in the field of Da'wah(دعوة), or in the field of politics, or in the field of jihad or whatever.

36
00:02:46,834 --> 00:02:50,269
This Ibadah(عبادة) is what prepares you for the work of the day.

37
00:02:51,235 --> 00:03:02,021
Because one of the worst things, that could erode your heart and put permanent scars in it is; the political work.

38
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:10,740
I mean; working in politics can really wear down the heart and destroy it,

39
00:03:11,806 --> 00:03:15,506
and take the Taqwa(تقوى) out of the heart like a drainage; it just take it out.

40
00:03:16,346 --> 00:03:19,798
So anyone; who's working in that field which is political,

41
00:03:20,224 --> 00:03:28,423
whether it is a king like, Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد); or a Khalifah(خليفه) like, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب); or a military general like, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

42
00:03:28,883 --> 00:03:37,109
You need that worship; you need that prayer of Qiyam-Al-Layl(قيام اليل) and Dhikr(ذكر), to keep you always on the right track.

43
00:03:38,163 --> 00:03:41,409
So that is the energy, that they use to go ahead.

44
00:03:41,743 --> 00:03:46,632
With the Kafir(كافر); Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is giving them energy to continue.

45
00:03:46,985 --> 00:03:48,545
Because this is very difficult work.

46
00:03:49,172 --> 00:03:57,118
But for the believer, if you do not have this Qiyam-Al-Layl(قيام اليل) and Dhikr(ذكر) of Allah and fasting; you could easily be misled and misguided.

47
00:03:59,011 --> 00:04:05,078
Because these are very difficult field to work in; you're dealing with many conflicting ideas and things,

48
00:04:05,705 --> 00:04:09,584
and it could take the concentration away from one's mind and heart.

49
00:04:09,657 --> 00:04:11,484
So that's why, they need this Ibadah(عبادة).

50
00:04:11,531 --> 00:04:14,271
And Sayidina Dawoodعليه السلام would pray one third of the night.

51
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:17,089
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب); I remind you once again with the story.

52
00:04:17,416 --> 00:04:25,138
When Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani(ابو مسلم ال-خولانى) came to deliver the news to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) that certain area in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) was opened.

53
00:04:25,405 --> 00:04:28,600
Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani(ابو مسلم ال-خولانى) came into Madinah(مَدِينَه) when it was the time of noon.

54
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,299
And it was the tradition of the Arabs to sleep at noon.

55
00:04:31,552 --> 00:04:32,499
Because it was very hot.

56
00:04:32,872 --> 00:04:35,862
Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani(ابو مسلم ال-خولانى) did not want to go and disturb Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

57
00:04:35,887 --> 00:04:36,938
So he went to the Masjid(مسجد).

58
00:04:37,805 --> 00:04:41,030
He felt that, maybe Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is sleeping; so I'll go to the Masjid(مسجد).

59
00:04:41,544 --> 00:04:50,493
He went to the Masjid(مسجد) and he gave out the news; he spread the news to the people that; We won! We were victorious.

60
00:04:51,213 --> 00:04:53,893
Somehow, the news reached to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

61
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:58,845
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) called Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani(ابو مسلم ال-خولانى), he told him;

62
00:04:58,870 --> 00:05:00,692
How come you didn't come and tell me first?

63
00:05:01,179 --> 00:05:02,423
Who should you report to?

64
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:03,386
To the Khalifah(خليفه)!

65
00:05:03,546 --> 00:05:04,811
You go and tell the people in the Masjid(مسجد).?

66
00:05:05,011 --> 00:05:06,305
You should come and tell me first.

67
00:05:06,745 --> 00:05:08,645
Why didn't you come and let me know?

68
00:05:09,345 --> 00:05:10,407
Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani(ابو مسلم ال-خولانى) said;

69
00:05:10,427 --> 00:05:15,874
Oh Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين)! I came into Madinah(مَدِينَه) when it was time of noon; so I did not want to disturb you.

70
00:05:16,094 --> 00:05:17,618
Because I thought that you were asleep.

71
00:05:19,278 --> 00:05:20,185
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

72
00:05:20,225 --> 00:05:27,531
هيهات هيهات انا نوم ،ان انمت بالنهار زيأت حق العباد، وان انمت باليل زیات حق الله

73
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:29,262
He said; How can I sleep!

74
00:05:29,769 --> 00:05:36,275
If I sleep during the daytime, I would not fulfill my duties toward the people; toward my nation.

75
00:05:36,708 --> 00:05:42,310
And if I sleep at night, I would not be able to fulfill my duties towards Allah.

76
00:05:42,984 --> 00:05:46,780
If I sleep at the daytime; I would not fulfill my duties towards the creation.

77
00:05:47,107 --> 00:05:51,742
And if I sleep at night; I would not be able to fill my duties towards the Creator.

78
00:05:52,389 --> 00:05:58,655
They said that, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب); when he became Khalifah(خليفه), he never slept the traditional way of sleeping on a bed with a blanket.

79
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:04,570
He would sleep sitting down, or leaning on a wall, or take a nap here and there,

80
00:06:05,557 --> 00:06:13,166
and keep on moving, keep on working; Mujahideen(مجاهدين); these were the graduates from the training of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

81
00:06:13,532 --> 00:06:17,579
Dawoodعليه السلام was very protective of his family.

82
00:06:17,879 --> 00:06:22,168
He would not allow any man to see his wives.

83
00:06:22,861 --> 00:06:25,604
And this is mentioned in a Hadith(حديث),

84
00:06:25,658 --> 00:06:34,821
so when he would leave his home, or palace, or whatever; he would close all the doors, and not allow any man to get in.

85
00:06:37,361 --> 00:06:45,067
Suddenly one day; the wife of Dawood(داؤد) sees a man in the middle of the house.

86
00:06:45,567 --> 00:06:47,513
There's a man in our home.

87
00:06:48,587 --> 00:06:48,947
She said;

88
00:06:48,967 --> 00:06:50,453
والله لنفتضحن بداود

89
00:06:50,473 --> 00:06:52,666
If Dawood(داؤد) knows about this; we're in big trouble.

90
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:54,655
How did this man get in?

91
00:06:55,055 --> 00:06:56,542
Dawoodعليه السلام did come.

92
00:06:57,255 --> 00:06:58,602
And he saw this man.

93
00:06:58,975 --> 00:07:00,373
And he said; Who are you?

94
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,686
The man said;

95
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:07,591
انا الذي لا هاب الملوك ، ولا يمتنع منى شئى

96
00:07:09,031 --> 00:07:15,613
He said; I am the one who never fears the kings; and nothing can run away from me.

97
00:07:17,273 --> 00:07:23,082
I'm the one, who does not fear the kings, and nothing can run away from me.

98
00:07:23,402 --> 00:07:24,976
Dawoodعليه السلام said;

99
00:07:25,122 --> 00:07:29,001
والله إذا ملك الموت . مرحبا بأمر الله

100
00:07:29,248 --> 00:07:34,221
In the name of Allah! You must be the angel of death; welcome with the decree of Allah.

101
00:07:35,714 --> 00:07:39,650
A king; he has everything, a person would want in this life.

102
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:45,277
I mean; we are holding to this world; holding so tight to this world for a few bucks, that we make here and there.

103
00:07:45,477 --> 00:07:47,237
 We don't really have much, none of us are kings.

104
00:07:48,350 --> 00:07:51,942
We don't have that much; and we're holding so tight to this world.

105
00:07:53,089 --> 00:07:57,669
For the small part of the world which is allocated for us, we became servants to it.

106
00:07:58,656 --> 00:08:05,864
And Dawoodعليه السلام is the king of the strongest nation of its time, and the Muslim ummah(امة) of that time; Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

107
00:08:06,097 --> 00:08:08,503
And when he saw the angel of death, he said; Welcome!

108
00:08:08,810 --> 00:08:09,830
 مرحبا بأمر الله

109
00:08:09,850 --> 00:08:13,348
Welcome with the decree of Allah, I'm ready! I'm ready to die!

110
00:08:13,528 --> 00:08:15,452
Because, I wasn't the king for the kingdom;

111
00:08:15,738 --> 00:08:17,631
I wasn't the king for the gold and silver;

112
00:08:17,877 --> 00:08:21,924
I wasn't the king to love this world; I was a king to serve Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

113
00:08:22,204 --> 00:08:24,174
I was doing this as a service for Allah.

114
00:08:25,227 --> 00:08:29,776
I'm doing it for you Oh Allah! If you want me to leave, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى I want to meet You.

115
00:08:30,656 --> 00:08:31,809
مرحبا بأمر الله

116
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:38,018
The Angel of Death took away the soul of Dawoodعليه السلام on the spot.

117
00:08:40,125 --> 00:08:51,955
Sulaimanعليه السلام; his son, ordered the birds to cover the body of Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد), and to provide shade for him from the sun,

118
00:08:52,662 --> 00:08:54,831
until they would finish the process of death.

119
00:08:55,911 --> 00:09:00,763
And when night-time came; Sulaiman(سليمان) ordered the birds to Protect him,

120
00:09:01,396 --> 00:09:12,172
and come closer to him, and to protect them with their wings, until they finish the process of making Dafan(دفن) of Sayidina Dawoodعليه السلام.

121
00:09:12,478 --> 00:09:17,228
And this shows you that, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made the birds servants for them.

122
00:09:18,341 --> 00:09:27,655
The one who worships Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and he's righteous towards Allah; Allah can make steel; iron soft in his hands; Dawoodعليه السلام.

123
00:09:28,262 --> 00:09:30,835
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى can have the birds serve him.

124
00:09:32,249 --> 00:09:37,457
This is the story of our beloved prophet of Allah, David; Dawoodعليه السلام.

125
00:09:39,004 --> 00:09:41,289
We start with the story of Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

126
00:09:43,036 --> 00:09:44,489
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

127
00:09:44,776 --> 00:09:54,095
وَدَاوُۥدَ وَسُلَيْمَٰنَ إِذْ يَحْكُمَانِ فِى ٱلْحَرْثِ إِذْ نَفَشَتْ فِيهِ غَنَمُ ٱلْقَوْمِ

128
00:09:54,308 --> 00:10:01,879
 إِذْ نَفَشَتْ فِيهِ غَنَمُ ٱلْقَوْمِ وَكُنَّا لِحُكْمِهِمْ شَٰهِدِينَ۝

129
00:10:02,126 --> 00:10:03,472
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

130
00:10:03,692 --> 00:10:09,906
And remember Dawood(داؤد) and Sulaiman(سليمان); when they gave judgment in the case of the field,

131
00:10:09,986 --> 00:10:17,250
in which the sheep of certain people had pastured at night, and We were witnesses to their judgment.

132
00:10:18,137 --> 00:10:19,597
There are two neighbours.

133
00:10:20,430 --> 00:10:24,090
One of them had a farm, and the other one had sheep.

134
00:10:26,337 --> 00:10:31,492
The owner of the sheep forgot to lock his gate at night-time.

135
00:10:32,252 --> 00:10:35,859
So the sheep, they went into the farm, and they enjoyed themselves.

136
00:10:37,172 --> 00:10:38,979
And they destroyed everything in the farm.

137
00:10:40,385 --> 00:10:49,014
The owner of the farm wakes up in the morning and sees that his farm is eaten and by his neighbour's goats or sheep.

138
00:10:49,781 --> 00:10:55,686
They went to Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد), to ask him to give his Hukum(حكم); his judgment.

139
00:10:57,446 --> 00:11:04,901
Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد) listen to both sides, and his Hukum(حكم) was; his judgment was that;

140
00:11:05,501 --> 00:11:10,186
the owner of the farm takes over the sheep.

141
00:11:11,799 --> 00:11:15,348
Because it was due to the carelessness of the owner of the sheep.

142
00:11:15,848 --> 00:11:21,291
The owner of the sheep should give up his sheep to the owner of the farm; as a compensation.

143
00:11:21,691 --> 00:11:24,491
You damaged his farm, give up the sheep; give it to him.

144
00:11:25,044 --> 00:11:28,070
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام was outside of the court.

145
00:11:28,470 --> 00:11:30,223
When they came out; he asked them; What happened?

146
00:11:30,597 --> 00:11:31,871
They told him; What was the Hukum(حكم).?

147
00:11:32,031 --> 00:11:37,502
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان), he took them back and he told his father; I have another Hukum(حكم).

148
00:11:38,815 --> 00:11:45,941
My Hukum(حكم) is that; the owner of the sheep, should give the owner of the farm; the sheep.

149
00:11:48,068 --> 00:11:55,643
The owner of the farm will keep the sheep with him, and make use of their milk; will drink from the milk.

150
00:11:56,223 --> 00:11:59,176
While, the owner of the sheep fixes the farm.

151
00:12:00,682 --> 00:12:07,712
And as soon as the farm is fixed and returned to its to its normal state that it was in,

152
00:12:08,545 --> 00:12:12,213
then the owner of the sheep takes back his sheep again.

153
00:12:13,866 --> 00:12:16,075
So the Fatwa(فتوى) of Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) is that;

154
00:12:16,442 --> 00:12:22,618
the sheep are given to the owner of the farm for a while, so that he can live off the milk of the sheep.

155
00:12:22,951 --> 00:12:26,573
While, the owner of the sheep fixes the problems caused by his sheep.

156
00:12:26,913 --> 00:12:31,824
As soon as the problem is fixed, and the farm is back to the state it was before;

157
00:12:32,117 --> 00:12:36,815
then he takes his sheep, and the owner of the farm goes back to his farm.

158
00:12:37,175 --> 00:12:41,055
And Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد) realize that this is the right Hukum(حكم), so he approved it.

159
00:12:41,375 --> 00:12:43,137
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in Qur'an;

160
00:12:43,191 --> 00:12:44,564
فَفَهَّمْنَٰهَا سُلَيْمَٰنَ ۚ

161
00:12:44,991 --> 00:12:47,562
We gave the right understanding to Sulaiman(سليمان).

162
00:12:48,962 --> 00:12:54,414
Judgment in court; Al-Qadha(ال قضا); it's not a matter of only knowing the law.

163
00:12:55,534 --> 00:12:57,348
Because both Dawood(داؤد) and Sulaiman(سليمان), they know the law.

164
00:12:57,368 --> 00:13:02,268
We cannot say that, Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد) did not know the Hukum(حكم); did not know the law; did not know the Shariah(شريعة).

165
00:13:02,681 --> 00:13:10,919
They both knew the law. But to apply the law; to apply the law in situations that is where people are different according to their understanding.

166
00:13:11,559 --> 00:13:20,263
Now Allahسُبحانه وتعالى makes it clear to us that both of them had the understanding in applying the Shariah(شريعة) of Allah.

167
00:13:20,816 --> 00:13:22,349
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى after he said;

168
00:13:22,429 --> 00:13:23,955
فَفَهَّمْنَٰهَا سُلَيْمَٰنَ ۚ

169
00:13:24,122 --> 00:13:25,086
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

170
00:13:25,126 --> 00:13:27,264
وَكُلًّا ءَاتَيْنَا حُكْمًا وَعِلْمًا ۚ

171
00:13:27,631 --> 00:13:31,398
We gave them both; knowledge and the right judgment.

172
00:13:31,878 --> 00:13:35,461
Both Dawood(داؤد) and Sulaiman(سليمان) had the knowledge, and had the right judgment.

173
00:13:35,701 --> 00:13:39,954
It is just that, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave this understanding to Sulaiman(سليمان) in these situations.

174
00:13:40,481 --> 00:13:43,146
And where was Sulaiman(سليمان) learning anyway; Who was training him?

175
00:13:43,366 --> 00:13:44,326
It was his father.

176
00:13:44,786 --> 00:13:46,066
I mean; he was learning from his father.

177
00:13:46,866 --> 00:13:50,882
But sometimes, the son can be better than the father in some things.

178
00:13:52,356 --> 00:14:00,698
But both of them, Dawood(داؤد) and Sulaiman(سليمان); Allahسُبحانه وتعالى blessed them with the law of Allah, and the ability to apply it.

179
00:14:01,151 --> 00:14:06,960
At this point I mentioned it again; not everyone who has the understanding of the law; know how to apply it.

180
00:14:08,187 --> 00:14:16,276
You could have memorized all of the laws; all of the books of Fiqh(فقه); all of the books of Hadith(حديث), but you might not know how to apply it.

181
00:14:16,403 --> 00:14:24,122
This is a Mowhibah(مؤهبه); it's a gift from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to some people, that they have the ability to apply the law in real situations.

182
00:14:25,169 --> 00:14:29,786
And this is something, that some of the Sahabahرضى الله عنهم were better than others in.

183
00:14:29,806 --> 00:14:39,058
And they excel like, for example; Sayidina Ali Ibn Abi Talib(سيدنا علي ابن ابي طالب) was famous among the Sahabah(صحابه) as being a very wise judge.

184
00:14:39,864 --> 00:14:45,910
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) used to get assistance from Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), and he would appoint him as a judge.

185
00:14:46,063 --> 00:14:49,050
This is an understanding that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gives to the people.

186
00:14:49,983 --> 00:14:56,077
There is another case that was presented to Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد).

187
00:14:56,450 --> 00:14:58,705
And this is in a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ).

188
00:14:59,318 --> 00:15:04,348
Two women disputed, what happened is; these two women were shepherds.

189
00:15:05,328 --> 00:15:09,366
So they went out with their sheep and they had their infants; the infants were the same age.

190
00:15:10,513 --> 00:15:18,082
And they left their infant somewhere, and they went talking or maybe shepherding; a wolf came and ate one of the infants.

191
00:15:18,815 --> 00:15:22,187
When the women came back, and they found that one of the infants is eaten.

192
00:15:22,887 --> 00:15:28,863
Both of them claim that, the infant who is alive belongs to them.

193
00:15:29,443 --> 00:15:31,376
Every one of them is saying; He's my son.

194
00:15:32,763 --> 00:15:35,161
And they fought with each other, and they couldn't solve the problem.

195
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:36,894
They went to Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد).

196
00:15:37,874 --> 00:15:41,216
Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد); he listened to both sides of the story.

197
00:15:41,349 --> 00:15:47,159
He made the judgment that; the child should go to the eldest of them; Al-Kubra(الكبرى).

198
00:15:48,346 --> 00:15:51,566
When they were leaving from the court; Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) asked them; What happened?

199
00:15:51,586 --> 00:15:52,793
They told them what happened.

200
00:15:53,239 --> 00:15:57,217
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said; Get me the child.

201
00:15:58,177 --> 00:16:00,091
And he said; Bring me a knife.

202
00:16:02,024 --> 00:16:03,677
So the woman said; What do you want to do with a knife?

203
00:16:03,877 --> 00:16:04,731
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said;

204
00:16:04,751 --> 00:16:11,422
If you're not able to solve the problem, and know who this child belongs to; I'm going to split the child in two, between you.

205
00:16:12,389 --> 00:16:16,110
The youngest woman immediately said; No! It belongs to her.

206
00:16:16,590 --> 00:16:17,283
It's her son.

207
00:16:18,430 --> 00:16:21,994
Sulaimanعليه السلام used this surprise against these two women.

208
00:16:23,261 --> 00:16:31,022
Because he knew that the mother would not want this to happen to her child, and reaction would immediately show on her.

209
00:16:31,569 --> 00:16:36,349
So Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) by this, was able to tell that the youngest one is the mother.

210
00:16:36,696 --> 00:16:39,043
The one who said; No, it belongs to the eldest one.

211
00:16:39,503 --> 00:16:41,065
Because she wanted to save her son.

212
00:16:41,292 --> 00:16:43,552
So she said; No, it belongs to her.

213
00:16:43,785 --> 00:16:46,145
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said; Then you take the child.

214
00:16:46,484 --> 00:16:48,931
And he gave it back to the youngest among them.

215
00:16:48,971 --> 00:16:59,913
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام inherited his father Dawood(داؤد).

216
00:17:00,007 --> 00:17:01,513
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

217
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:05,301
وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ وَسُلَيْمَانَ عِلْمًا ۖ

218
00:17:06,121 --> 00:17:09,148
We have given knowledge to David and Sulaiman(سليمان).

219
00:17:09,448 --> 00:17:19,369
Knowledge is one of the things that, we could become proud with and it is similar to money.

220
00:17:19,429 --> 00:17:24,816
We always tend to give credit to our hard work.

221
00:17:25,762 --> 00:17:32,458
I am successful because, I studied hard; or I'm rich because, I worked hard.

222
00:17:35,211 --> 00:17:45,266
But with anything; whether it is money, wealth or knowledge; all; all of the credit goes back to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

223
00:17:46,079 --> 00:17:48,666
 It is Allah who made it possible for you to study.

224
00:17:50,019 --> 00:17:52,616
It is Allah who made it possible for you to work hard.

225
00:17:52,916 --> 00:17:58,129
Allah could have inflicted you with the disease, and no matter how hard worker you are; you wouldn't be able to do anything.

226
00:17:59,149 --> 00:18:02,952
So it's a Tawfeeq(توفيق) from Allah; Allah is the one who made it possible for you to do this.

227
00:18:03,378 --> 00:18:07,064
Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد) and Sulaiman(سليمان); who were at the highest levels of knowledge in their time.

228
00:18:07,084 --> 00:18:08,616
Nobody else had more knowledge than they did.

229
00:18:09,109 --> 00:18:10,749
Nobody had more understanding than they did.

230
00:18:10,809 --> 00:18:12,049
They were the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah.

231
00:18:12,842 --> 00:18:16,236
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى say that; We gave them knowledge; What was their response?

232
00:18:16,259 --> 00:18:16,586
They said;

233
00:18:16,626 --> 00:18:21,051
وَقَالَا الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي فَضَّلَنَا عَلَىٰ كَثِيرٍ مِّنْ عِبَادِهِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

234
00:18:21,618 --> 00:18:30,024
They said; All the praises and thanks be to Allah, Who has preferred us above many of His believing slaves.

235
00:18:30,891 --> 00:18:33,026
So the blessing is from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

236
00:18:33,292 --> 00:18:35,556
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the One, Who is thanked.

237
00:18:36,296 --> 00:18:39,961
And the issue of thanking, is a very, very important Ibadah(عبادة).

238
00:18:40,288 --> 00:18:43,688
Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبنِ ألقَيِّم) says that, There are two wings for the bird;

239
00:18:43,928 --> 00:18:45,963
one of them is Shukr(شكر) and one of them is Sabr(صبر).

240
00:18:47,837 --> 00:18:49,883
We have to have these two wings.

241
00:18:50,263 --> 00:18:52,915
On one side we have thanks; and on one side we have patience.

242
00:18:53,309 --> 00:18:55,622
If anything good happens to us; we think Allah.

243
00:18:56,129 --> 00:18:58,669
If anything bad happens to us; we have patience.

244
00:18:59,342 --> 00:19:02,801
وَوَرِثَ سُلَيْمَٰنُ دَاوُۥدَ ۖ

245
00:19:03,067 --> 00:19:05,507
And Sulaiman(سليمان) inherited David.

246
00:19:06,767 --> 00:19:09,080
What did Sulaiman(سليمان) inherit from his father?

247
00:19:09,933 --> 00:19:14,786
He Inherited from him; An-Nabuwwah(اَلنَّبُوَّة); Prophet-hood and Kingdom.

248
00:19:16,553 --> 00:19:21,982
It is not the wealth; because Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); they do not leave behind wealth.

249
00:19:22,535 --> 00:19:27,020
What they leave behind is; Sadaqah(صدقة), but it is the kingdom and it is the Nabuwwah(نبُوَّة) the Prophethood.

250
00:19:28,087 --> 00:19:34,237
 Allahسُبحانه وتعالى tested Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام with some tests.

251
00:19:35,311 --> 00:19:41,195
إِذْ عُرِضَ عَلَيْهِ بِٱلْعَشِىِّ ٱلصَّٰفِنَٰتُ ٱلْجِيَادُ۝

252
00:19:41,688 --> 00:19:48,911
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; When there were displayed before him in the afternoon; well trained horses of the highest breed.

253
00:19:49,904 --> 00:19:56,270
This was like an army parade in front of Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان), to show his army.

254
00:19:56,596 --> 00:20:00,372
So they were marching the horses in front of him, and he was inspecting the horses.

255
00:20:02,005 --> 00:20:05,452
When he was inspecting the horses, he got busy with that.

256
00:20:05,872 --> 00:20:08,674
And the time of Salah(صلوة) passed, and he missed the Salah(صلوة).

257
00:20:08,962 --> 00:20:19,029
فَقَالَ إِنِّىٓ أَحْبَبْتُ حُبَّ ٱلْخَيْرِ عَن ذِكْرِ رَبِّى حَتَّىٰ تَوَارَتْ بِٱلْحِجَابِ۝

258
00:20:19,416 --> 00:20:24,618
And he said; Alas! I did love the good, instead of remembering my Lord

259
00:20:24,775 --> 00:20:27,661
in my Asr(عصر) prayer, this is in Paranthesis;

260
00:20:28,095 --> 00:20:32,964
till the time was over, and the sun had hidden in the veil of night.

261
00:20:33,311 --> 00:20:39,529
Sulaiman(سليمان) was inspecting these horses, and the time of Maghrib(مغرب) came before he prayed Asr(عصر); So, he missed Asr(عصر).

262
00:20:41,076 --> 00:20:42,456
The next Ayah(آية) says;

263
00:20:42,796 --> 00:20:50,145
رُدُّوهَا عَلَىَّ ۖ فَطَفِقَ مَسْحًۢا بِٱلسُّوقِ وَٱلْأَعْنَاقِ۝

264
00:20:50,792 --> 00:20:58,903
Then he said; Bring these horses back to me, and he began to pass his hand over their legs and their necks.

265
00:20:59,310 --> 00:21:01,676
There are two opinions, given in the Tafseer(تفسير) of this Ayah(آية).

266
00:21:02,083 --> 00:21:04,171
And both of them are nothing more than opinions.

267
00:21:04,664 --> 00:21:12,749
There's no strong Hadith(حديث) or evidence, that either one of them is right, or maybe if both of them could be wrong.

268
00:21:13,936 --> 00:21:16,052
The two opinions are; one of them is that;

269
00:21:16,372 --> 00:21:22,742
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان); he passed his hands over the horses, as an honoring for these horses of Jihad(جهاد).

270
00:21:23,749 --> 00:21:24,897
The other opinion is that;

271
00:21:24,937 --> 00:21:31,079
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) who was upset; because the horses were the cause of distracting him from Salah(صلوة).

272
00:21:31,366 --> 00:21:34,472
So he cut off their necks, and killed them.

273
00:21:36,152 --> 00:21:40,985
Ibn Jarir At-Tabari(ابن جرير ألطبري) refuses to accept the second opinion, because he says;

274
00:21:41,338 --> 00:21:46,636
How come Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) would blame the horses, who are innocent, for this.

275
00:21:47,569 --> 00:21:50,142
So there's no way to choose any one of the opinions.

276
00:21:50,162 --> 00:21:53,631
And then the first opinion; what does it mean by passing his hand over them?

277
00:21:54,704 --> 00:21:57,651
But the lesson that we learn from the Ayah(آية) is clear.

278
00:21:57,671 --> 00:22:00,042
And first of all, we believe in the Ayaat(آيات) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

279
00:22:00,062 --> 00:22:04,455
And the lesson is clear that, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى was testing him.

280
00:22:04,475 --> 00:22:08,368
And this test did also happen to Rasool Allah ﷺ in one of the battles.

281
00:22:08,681 --> 00:22:13,633
Rasool Allah ﷺ was busy with fighting, and they missed the Salah(صلوة), and Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

282
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:17,907
قاتل هم الله او لعنهم الله شغلونا عن الصلاة

283
00:22:18,333 --> 00:22:22,329
May Allah curse them! or May Allah fight them! They have distracted us from Salah(صلوة).

284
00:22:23,489 --> 00:22:27,222
And Rasool Allah ﷺ could not pray until, the sun has already set.

285
00:22:28,915 --> 00:22:31,634
Some of the Ulama(عُلَمَا) derive a Hukum(حكم) from this؛

286
00:22:31,954 --> 00:22:38,663
that If the battle ground allows you to pray Salat-ul-Khauf(صلوةالخوف), then pray Salat-ul-Khauf(صلوةالخوف).

287
00:22:39,210 --> 00:22:47,439
In case, the fighting is so vicious and tough, and you're not even able to pray Salat-ul-Khauf(صلوةالخوف); then you can delay it and pray it when the battle is over.

288
00:22:47,946 --> 00:22:51,172
This is the Hukum(حكم) of some of the Ulama(عُلَمَا) derived from this Hadith(حديث).

289
00:22:52,099 --> 00:22:55,325
Another test happened to Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان). Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

290
00:22:55,352 --> 00:23:06,203
وَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا سُلَيْمَٰنَ وَأَلْقَيْنَا عَلَىٰ كُرْسِيِّهِۦ جَسَدًا ثُمَّ أَنَابَ۝

291
00:23:06,617 --> 00:23:17,702
And We indeed, did try Solomon, and he placed on his throne; Jasadan(جَسَدًا), but he did return to Allah with obedience and repentance.

292
00:23:18,155 --> 00:23:23,991
There is a Hadith(حديث) that is Sahih(صحيح), which could explain what this Ayah(آية) means.

293
00:23:24,517 --> 00:23:26,116
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

294
00:23:26,656 --> 00:23:36,342
قالَ سُلَيْمَانُ بنُ دَاوُدَ: لَأَطُوفَنَّ اللَّيْلَةَ علَى سَبْعِينَ امْرَأَةً، تَحْمِلُ كُلُّ امْرَأَةٍ فَارِسًا يُجَاهِدُ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ،

295
00:23:36,609 --> 00:23:45,698
فَقالَ له صَاحِبُهُ: إنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ، فَلَمْ يَقُلْ، ولَمْ تَحْمِلْ شيئًا إلَّا واحِدًا، سَاقِطًا أَحَدُ شِقَّيْهِ،

296
00:23:46,145 --> 00:23:49,910
فَقالَ النبيُّ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ: لو قالَهَا لَجَاهَدُوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ

297
00:23:50,617 --> 00:23:54,137
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام in this Hadith(حديث); Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

298
00:23:54,257 --> 00:24:01,713
He said that, he will pass by all of his 70 wives.

299
00:24:02,893 --> 00:24:06,065
Another Hadith(حديث), it is 90, and this Hadith(حديث) is Sahih(صحيح) in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

300
00:24:06,739 --> 00:24:10,562
So he's going to sleep with every one of his wives.

301
00:24:12,642 --> 00:24:21,718
And he did that with the intention of; all of the children that will be born, they will fight in the sake of Allah.

302
00:24:21,958 --> 00:24:23,469
He wants to have Mujahideen(مجاهدين);

303
00:24:23,729 --> 00:24:29,065
so he decided that, he will sleep with every one of his wife; So that, she could give birth to a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) in the sake of Allah.

304
00:24:30,295 --> 00:24:34,834
His associates told him; In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله)! Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) did not say, In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله).

305
00:24:36,307 --> 00:24:38,819
And he went ahead, and slept with every one of the wives.

306
00:24:38,859 --> 00:24:42,666
None of them became pregnant except, one of them.

307
00:24:42,999 --> 00:24:45,584
And then; she delivered half a child.

308
00:24:45,764 --> 00:24:50,824
Somehow, it was mutilated, and only half of the child was remaining; and it was a dead body.

309
00:24:51,277 --> 00:24:54,996
And this is the meaning of the Ayah(آية); We tested Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان); It's a trial from Allah.

310
00:24:55,099 --> 00:24:56,913
وَأَلْقَيْنَا عَلَىٰ كُرْسِيِّهِۦ جَسَدًا

311
00:24:57,226 --> 00:24:59,741
We threw on his throne, a dead body.

312
00:24:59,888 --> 00:25:00,761
ثُمَّ أَنَابَ۝

313
00:25:00,781 --> 00:25:02,541
Then, he returned to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

314
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:07,956
It's a test from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for him; to say, In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله)!

315
00:25:08,329 --> 00:25:13,615
And therefore, whenever we want to do something in the future; we always need to tie it to the will of Allah.

316
00:25:13,689 --> 00:25:15,562
Because nothing can happen, if Allah does not will.

317
00:25:16,595 --> 00:25:20,537
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام; as Allah says; Returned to Allah.

318
00:25:20,624 --> 00:25:21,391
ثُمَّ أَنَابَ۝

319
00:25:21,904 --> 00:25:23,224
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

320
00:25:23,357 --> 00:25:37,403
قَالَ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي وَهَبْ لِي مُلْكًا لَّا يَنبَغِي لِأَحَدٍ مِّن بَعْدِي ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ الْوَهَّابُ۝

321
00:25:37,576 --> 00:25:39,752
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said; Oh Allah! Forgive me.

322
00:25:40,725 --> 00:25:44,005
And after he asked Allah for forgiveness, he made a Dua(دُعَا).

323
00:25:44,338 --> 00:25:49,924
He said; Oh Allah! Give me a kingdom that will occur to nobody else after me.

324
00:25:50,144 --> 00:25:59,080
My Lord! Forgive me; and bestow upon me a kingdom such as shall not belong to any other after me; verily You are the bestower.

325
00:25:59,533 --> 00:26:04,713
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) is not asking kingdom, for the sake of kingdom; that is not the acture of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

326
00:26:05,387 --> 00:26:10,379
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) is asking for a kingdom, that would be a miracle; that would be his miracle.

327
00:26:10,699 --> 00:26:13,286
So the miracle of Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) would be his kingdom.

328
00:26:14,079 --> 00:26:16,714
Because every Nabi(نَبِي) Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gives him a miracle.

329
00:26:17,334 --> 00:26:22,887
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) asked Allah to give him a kingdom that will be unique; different from any other.

330
00:26:23,321 --> 00:26:27,030
And that would be the miracle of Sulaiman(سليمان); and we will see that it was truly a miracle.

331
00:26:27,684 --> 00:26:34,437
And Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان); no other person, Nabi(نَبِي) or not a Nabi(نَبِي), was given a kingdom similar to Sulaiman(سليمان).

332
00:26:34,462 --> 00:26:36,364
The kingdom of Sulaiman(سليمان) was unique.

333
00:26:37,970 --> 00:26:41,356
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى accepted the Dua(دُعَا) of Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان). Allah says;

334
00:26:41,689 --> 00:26:50,260
فَسَخَّرْنَا لَهُ ٱلرِّيحَ تَجْرِى بِأَمْرِهِۦ رُخَآءً حَيْثُ أَصَابَ۝

335
00:26:50,660 --> 00:26:56,315
So We subjected to him the wind; it blew gently to his order, wherever he willed.

336
00:26:56,355 --> 00:26:58,695
And we're going to talk about some other things in this kingdom.

337
00:26:58,882 --> 00:27:02,011
But first, let me read to you this Ayah(آية);

338
00:27:03,371 --> 00:27:15,168
وَوَرِثَ سُلَيْمَٰنُ دَاوُۥدَ ۖ وَقَالَ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ عُلِّمْنَا مَنطِقَ ٱلطَّيْرِ وَأُوتِينَا مِن كُلِّ شَىْءٍ ۖ

339
00:27:15,742 --> 00:27:20,874
إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَهُوَ ٱلْفَضْلُ ٱلْمُبِينُ۝

340
00:27:21,747 --> 00:27:23,120
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said;

341
00:27:23,487 --> 00:27:30,706
Oh mankind! We have been taught the language of birds, and on us have been bestowed all things.

342
00:27:31,219 --> 00:27:32,526
What does all things mean?

343
00:27:32,973 --> 00:27:36,259
Some of these things that the Ayah(آية) talked about is; Number one;

344
00:27:36,425 --> 00:27:37,032
Wind.

345
00:27:37,432 --> 00:27:41,212
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) had control over the wind for distance of a month.

346
00:27:42,332 --> 00:27:48,324
So he can use wind to travel for him, and accomplish things, a distance of a month.

347
00:27:48,591 --> 00:27:57,809
That's the span, that Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) had control over; distance of a month; that is the area of his control.

348
00:27:58,329 --> 00:27:59,815
Number one; control over wind.

349
00:28:00,281 --> 00:28:08,033
وَٱلشَّيَٰطِينَ كُلَّ بَنَّآءٍۢ وَغَوَّاصٍۢ۝

350
00:28:08,233 --> 00:28:13,932
And also the devils from the Jinn(جِن), every kind of builder and diver.

351
00:28:14,552 --> 00:28:22,853
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made the Shayateen(شَيَاطِين); the Devils, servants with Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

352
00:28:23,653 --> 00:28:27,192
And he would command them, with whatever order he want.

353
00:28:27,252 --> 00:28:31,246
Some of them would dive in the oceans, and some of them would build for him.

354
00:28:31,426 --> 00:28:33,275
And there's other Ayaat(آيات) that talk about this.

355
00:28:34,155 --> 00:28:37,897
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى also taught him the language of birds.

356
00:28:38,224 --> 00:28:43,216
And we also know from another Ayah(آية); that he knew the language of; the ants.

357
00:28:44,263 --> 00:28:45,476
And the other Ayah(آية);

358
00:28:46,096 --> 00:28:48,043
وَأَسَلْنَا لَهُ عَيْنَ الْقِطْرِ ۖ

359
00:28:49,276 --> 00:28:54,064
And We made a fountain of brass to flow for him.

360
00:28:55,264 --> 00:28:59,315
This was a fountain Allah-u-Aa'lam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ) how; but it would flow with brass.

361
00:29:00,002 --> 00:29:05,024
We know that his father, Dawoodعليه السلام had the ability to mold iron; steel.

362
00:29:05,364 --> 00:29:09,889
With Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان); Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided him with a fountain of brass.

363
00:29:09,956 --> 00:29:13,987
This brass would come out molten; he can mold it in whatever form he wants.

364
00:29:14,714 --> 00:29:21,516
وَمِنَ الْجِنِّ مَن يَعْمَلُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ بِإِذْنِ رَبِّهِ ۖ

365
00:29:21,736 --> 00:29:29,385
وَمَن يَزِغْ مِنْهُمْ عَنْ أَمْرِنَا نُذِقْهُ مِنْ عَذَابِ السَّعِييرِ۝

366
00:29:29,945 --> 00:29:34,440
And there were Jinn(جِن), that worked in front of him, by the leave of his Lord,

367
00:29:34,821 --> 00:29:42,644
and whomsoever of them turned aside from our command; we shall cause him to taste the torment of the blazing fire.

368
00:29:42,958 --> 00:29:46,686
Anyone of these Jinn(جِن), who would go against the order of Sulaiman(سليمان); would be punished.

369
00:29:47,386 --> 00:30:01,343
يَعْمَلُونَ لَهُۥ مَا يَشَآءُ مِن مَّحَٰرِيبَ وَتَمَٰثِيلَ وَجِفَانٍۢ كَٱلْجَوَابِ وَقُدُورٍۢ رَّاسِيَٰتٍ ۚ

370
00:30:01,629 --> 00:30:11,758
ٱعْمَلُوٓاْ ءَالَ دَااوُۥدَ شُكْرًا ۚ وَقَلِيلٌ مِّنْ عِبَادِىَ ٱلشَّكُورُ۝

371
00:30:12,091 --> 00:30:13,252
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

372
00:30:13,372 --> 00:30:24,530
They worked for him what he desired; making high rooms, images, basins, as large as resolvers, and cooking cauldrons fixed in their places.

373
00:30:24,790 --> 00:30:28,756
These are things that the Jinn(جِن) would do for Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

374
00:30:29,443 --> 00:30:30,328
And then, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

375
00:30:30,348 --> 00:30:32,188
ٱعْمَلُوٓاْ ءَالَ دَاوُۥدَ شُكْرًا ۚ

376
00:30:33,428 --> 00:30:39,139
Allah here, is commanding the family of Dawood(داؤد); Dawood(داؤد) and his son, to give thanks.

377
00:30:39,252 --> 00:30:42,464
But notice here, an important word in the Ayah(آية).

378
00:30:44,544 --> 00:30:45,530
What does the Ayah(آية) says;

379
00:30:45,550 --> 00:30:46,817
ٱعْمَلُوٓاْ

380
00:30:48,437 --> 00:30:53,359
We always think of thanks as a word, to say; Alhamdulillah(اَلْحَمْدُ لله)!

381
00:30:53,972 --> 00:30:58,051
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is saying in the Ayah(آية); and act with thanks.

382
00:30:58,071 --> 00:30:59,258
ٱعْمَلُوٓاْ شُكْرًا ۚ

383
00:31:00,385 --> 00:31:04,082
So thanking Allah is not only through the word; it is also through the actions.

384
00:31:04,435 --> 00:31:04,969
عَمَل

385
00:31:05,089 --> 00:31:07,589
ٱعْمَلُوٓاْ ءَالَ دَاوُۥدَ شُكْرًا ۚ

386
00:31:08,029 --> 00:31:11,228
Act with gratitude, and thanks to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

387
00:31:11,621 --> 00:31:13,461
So Shukr(شكر) needs action.

388
00:31:15,034 --> 00:31:17,310
You thank Allahسُبحانه وتعالى through your actions.

389
00:31:17,877 --> 00:31:18,497
And then, Allah says;

390
00:31:18,517 --> 00:31:19,737
وَقَلِيلٌ مِّنْ عِبَادِىَ ٱلشَّكُورُ۝

391
00:31:19,757 --> 00:31:23,770
Only a few of my servants are thankful and grateful.

392
00:31:24,890 --> 00:31:31,442
Rasool Allah ﷺ was praying, and he started making moves in a Salah(صلوة).

393
00:31:32,629 --> 00:31:35,166
So the Sahabahرضى الله عنهم asked Rasool Allah ﷺ; What were you doing?

394
00:31:35,659 --> 00:31:43,379
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Ash-Shaytan(الشَّيْطَانْ) came in front of my face; and he wanted to distract me from my Salah(صلوة).

395
00:31:43,666 --> 00:31:45,600
یلبس علیہ قراۃ القرآن

396
00:31:45,625 --> 00:31:49,134
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) was trying to confuse Rasool Allah ﷺ and his Qirah(قراة).

397
00:31:51,614 --> 00:31:58,503
Rasool Allah ﷺ pushed him first, he came back; push him a second time, he came back; pushed him a third time, the Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came back;

398
00:31:58,830 --> 00:32:00,957
Rasool Allah ﷺ grabbed him and chocked him.

399
00:32:01,377 --> 00:32:05,906
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I felt his saliva dripping on my hand.

400
00:32:06,726 --> 00:32:07,866
He choked him so hard.

401
00:32:08,279 --> 00:32:09,619
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

402
00:32:09,659 --> 00:32:16,683
And I was about to bring him forward, and tie him to a pillar in the Masjid(مسجد) so that the kids could play with.

403
00:32:17,163 --> 00:32:19,670
Throw things at him, and he's tied to a pillar.

404
00:32:20,490 --> 00:32:26,285
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; But I didn't do so; because I remember the Dua(دُعَا) of my brother Sulaiman(سليمان), when he said;

405
00:32:26,305 --> 00:32:29,223
Oh Allah! Give me a kingdom that will occur to no one else.

406
00:32:30,310 --> 00:32:31,303
What does this mean?

407
00:32:31,850 --> 00:32:36,609
Rasool Allah ﷺ was about to take control of this Jinn(جِن); this Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ), and tie it to the Masjid(مسجد).

408
00:32:37,002 --> 00:32:38,534
But the reason, why he didn't do so،

409
00:32:38,559 --> 00:32:43,163
is because; he remembered that this is something that was unique with Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان).

410
00:32:44,276 --> 00:32:47,946
The control over Jinn(جِن) was something unique given to Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان).

411
00:32:47,992 --> 00:32:49,906
Nobody else had the control over the Jinn(جِن).

412
00:32:50,339 --> 00:32:51,852
And that's why, Rasool Allah ﷺ released the Jinn(جِن);

413
00:32:51,879 --> 00:32:56,385
because he knew that, that's something that belongs to the uniqueness of the Kingdom of Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان).

414
00:32:56,531 --> 00:33:04,074
The control of the wind; the control of the Jinn(جِن); the ability to speak the language of the bird and the ant;

415
00:33:04,227 --> 00:33:07,540
these are some things that were unique with Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

416
00:33:07,774 --> 00:33:11,823
And he made a Dua(دُعَا) to Allah and Allah promised him that your kingdom will be unique.

417
00:33:13,209 --> 00:33:16,782
And that's the uniqueness of the kingdom of Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

418
00:33:17,295 --> 00:33:19,915
We talk about the Dua(دُعَا) of Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان).

419
00:33:20,542 --> 00:33:30,198
We would talk about one of the major events or the accomplishments of Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام,

420
00:33:30,564 --> 00:33:36,990
and that was the rebuilding and expansion of Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(مسجد الاقصى); the furthest mosque.

421
00:33:38,903 --> 00:33:44,132
Contrary to the belief of Jews; it is not Sulaiman(سليمان) who established the so called temple; they call it the temple.

422
00:33:44,152 --> 00:33:45,746
It's not a temple; it’s a Masjid(مسجد).

423
00:33:46,093 --> 00:33:48,860
They say; Sulaiman(سليمان) is the one, who built the temple.

424
00:33:48,900 --> 00:33:50,426
They call it; Solomon's temple.

425
00:33:50,633 --> 00:33:51,040
No!

426
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:53,736
The Masjid Al-Aqsa(مسجد الاقصى) was not established by Sulaiman(سليمان).

427
00:33:53,822 --> 00:33:54,749
Who's the one who built it?

428
00:33:55,069 --> 00:33:57,002
Sayidina Yaqubعليه السلام.

429
00:33:57,749 --> 00:34:01,599
Because in the Hadith(حديث), Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling Abu Dhar(ابو زر);

430
00:34:01,619 --> 00:34:05,100
that the first Masjid(مسجد) that was built is; Al-Masjid Al-Haram(المسجد الحرام); Al-Ka'bah(الكعبه).

431
00:34:05,356 --> 00:34:06,767
That was the first house that was built.

432
00:34:07,087 --> 00:34:09,214
Abu Dhar(ابو زر) said; And then what next?

433
00:34:09,354 --> 00:34:12,882
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; The furthest mosque; Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(المسجد الاقصى);

434
00:34:13,236 --> 00:34:14,896
وبينهما اربعون سنه

435
00:34:15,016 --> 00:34:21,318
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; And then the furthest mosque, and that was built by Sayidina Isra'il; Yaqubعليه السلام,

436
00:34:21,578 --> 00:34:27,844
and between the time of building Al-Ka'bah(الكعبه) and the furthest mosque is 40 years, and that's mentioned in the Hadith(حديث).

437
00:34:28,351 --> 00:34:32,151
What Sulaiman(سليمان) did is that; he expanded it or rebuilt it.

438
00:34:32,951 --> 00:34:41,610
After he finished the building of a Masjid Al-Aqsa(مسجد الاقصى); he made a Dua(دُعَا) to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and he asked Allah for three things.

439
00:34:44,203 --> 00:34:56,787
يقول صلى الله عليه وسلم: إن سليمان بن داود عليهما السلام ، سأل الله ثلاثا فأعطاه اثنتين ، ونحن نرجو أن تكون له الثالثة ؛

440
00:34:57,247 --> 00:35:01,898
فسأله حكما يصادف حكمه ، فأعطاه إياه ،

441
00:35:02,525 --> 00:35:03,814
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

442
00:35:03,934 --> 00:35:08,258
Sulaiman(سليمان) asked Allah for three things, Allah has given him two; Allah granted him two.

443
00:35:08,631 --> 00:35:11,724
And we hope that Allah has granted him the third.

444
00:35:12,598 --> 00:35:14,590
Sulaiman(سليمان) asked Allah, number one;

445
00:35:14,617 --> 00:35:15,694
To give him a Hukm(حکم)

446
00:35:15,719 --> 00:35:16,508
 يصادف حكمه

447
00:35:16,548 --> 00:35:20,740
To give him judgment that will be the same as the judgment of Allah.

448
00:35:22,060 --> 00:35:28,284
Meaning that; Sulaiman(سليمان) asked Allah to make his judgment according to what Allah wants; what pleases Allah.

449
00:35:29,198 --> 00:35:31,598
So whatever I would judge, that would be the right judgment.

450
00:35:31,678 --> 00:35:33,546
That is what Allah is pleased with.

451
00:35:34,473 --> 00:35:35,560
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

452
00:35:35,580 --> 00:35:36,440
فأعطاه إياه ،

453
00:35:36,466 --> 00:35:38,806
Allah has given him that; He was granted that Dua(دُعَا).

454
00:35:39,826 --> 00:35:40,998
The second Dua(دُعَا);

455
00:35:42,425 --> 00:35:46,365
وسأله ملكا لا ينبغي لأحد من بعده ، فأعطاه إياه ،

456
00:35:47,292 --> 00:35:52,001
And he asked Allah to give him a kingdom that will occur to nobody else; a unique kingdom.

457
00:35:52,421 --> 00:35:57,219
Rasool Ullah says; And Allah has given Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان); granted him that Dua(دُعَا).

458
00:35:57,699 --> 00:35:58,833
The third Dua(دُعَا);

459
00:35:59,379 --> 00:36:07,118
وسأله أيَّما رجلٍ خرج من بيته لا يريد إلا الصلاة في هذا المسجد

460
00:36:07,544 --> 00:36:11,148
خرج من خطيئته مثل يوم ولدته أمه

461
00:36:11,661 --> 00:36:16,308
فنحن نرجو أن يكون الله عز وجل قد أعطاه إياه

462
00:36:17,161 --> 00:36:20,928
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; And the third Dua(دُعَا) of Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) was that;

463
00:36:20,968 --> 00:36:29,150
If any man leaves his home with no intention other than praying in Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(المسجد الاقصى); the furthest mosque,

464
00:36:29,723 --> 00:36:39,566
than Oh Allah! Take him out of the Masjid(مسجد), as if he has left out with no sins just like the day he was born.

465
00:36:40,559 --> 00:36:44,159
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says; And we ask Allah that He has given him that Dua(دُعَا).

466
00:36:44,385 --> 00:36:49,620
So this Dua(دُعَا) was done by Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) and it was repeated by Sayidina Rasool Allah ﷺ;

467
00:36:49,846 --> 00:36:52,388
and we expect that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will accept that Dua(دُعَا).

468
00:36:52,688 --> 00:36:53,964
Therefore, the Ulama(عُلَمَا) say,

469
00:36:54,204 --> 00:36:58,377
that if you leave from your home with no intention other than praying in Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(المسجد الاقصى);

470
00:36:58,604 --> 00:37:02,050
if you go there and pray two Raka'ah(ركعه) with the sincerity,

471
00:37:02,377 --> 00:37:07,918
by the time you leave the door of the Masjid(مسجد); you would be leaving as if you were born with no sins.

472
00:37:10,125 --> 00:37:13,638
So we ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to grant us a Salah(صلوة) in Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(المسجد الاقصى)

473
00:37:14,238 --> 00:37:23,539
and to free it from al Al-Yahood(ال يهود); the Jewish terrorists who have taken over the third holy site of Islam; Masjid Al-Aqsa(مسجد الاقصى).

474
00:37:23,559 --> 00:37:31,335
We ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to free it from their hands and to give it back to the Ummah(امة) of Islam; the ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

475
00:37:31,788 --> 00:37:34,804
Allah says and these Ayaat(آيات) are from Surat-ul Namal(سورة النمل).

476
00:37:35,017 --> 00:37:38,657
Surat-ul Namal(سورة النمل) mentions a portion of the story of Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان).

477
00:37:39,464 --> 00:37:41,084
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

478
00:37:41,977 --> 00:37:51,814
وَحُشِرَ لِسُلَيْمَٰنَ جُنُودُهُۥ مِنَ ٱلْجِنِّ وَٱلْإِنسِ وَٱلطَّيْرِ فَهُمْ يُيُوزَعُونَ۝

479
00:37:52,707 --> 00:37:54,201
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

480
00:37:54,421 --> 00:38:07,049
And there were gathered before Sulaiman(سليمان); Solomon, his soldiers of Jinn(جِن), and men, and birds, and they were all set in battle order.

481
00:38:08,182 --> 00:38:09,296
وَحُشِرَ

482
00:38:10,002 --> 00:38:14,257
Hushira(حُشِرَ) means; assembled and gathered in one place.

483
00:38:14,684 --> 00:38:19,124
Hushira(حُشِرَ); when you have things in different areas and you bring them together that's called Hashar(حَشَر).

484
00:38:20,077 --> 00:38:23,003
That's why the Day of Judgment is called yaum-al-hashr(يوم الحشر).

485
00:38:23,636 --> 00:38:28,690
Because you have people all over the world, and you're bringing them to one place; you're assembling them together.

486
00:38:29,090 --> 00:38:33,695
Over here Sayidina Sulaiman علیہ السلام is gathering his army.

487
00:38:34,788 --> 00:38:43,521
And the Ayah(آية) says that, he has a battalion of men; soldiers, and a battalion of Jinn(جِن), and the squadron of birds.

488
00:38:43,774 --> 00:38:52,915
Imagine that army, that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put under his command and control, creation, which nobody else had control over.

489
00:38:53,822 --> 00:39:01,314
So Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام had control over the Jinn(جِن) or at least part of them or maybe all, Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ).

490
00:39:01,788 --> 00:39:10,589
And he also had control over this, army of birds, that would join him in his army.

491
00:39:10,922 --> 00:39:14,821
Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ)! What uses he would find for them?

492
00:39:15,075 --> 00:39:17,908
But they were part of his army.

493
00:39:19,088 --> 00:39:20,275
فَهُمْ يُوزَعُونَ۝

494
00:39:21,101 --> 00:39:31,574
Yuzaoon(يُوزَعُونَ) Because the army is so large, and so huge and vast, and contains thousands or maybe millions of soldiers.

495
00:39:32,527 --> 00:39:42,743
They had to have security guards to monitor the army, and to make sure that all the army is there and we're not leaving anybody behind.

496
00:39:43,436 --> 00:39:50,676
So they have to have the security around the army to make sure that everyone is moving together because it's like an ocean moving.

497
00:39:51,569 --> 00:39:56,388
They were marching, and they came into a valley.

498
00:39:58,254 --> 00:40:01,688
This Valley was occupied by ants.

499
00:40:03,441 --> 00:40:05,263
There are many ants in this valley.

500
00:40:05,810 --> 00:40:09,823
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى called it wadiy namal(وَادِ ٱلنَّمْلِ); the valley of ants.

501
00:40:09,863 --> 00:40:13,985
There were so many ants living in that valley; it was called the Valley of ants.

502
00:40:15,039 --> 00:40:20,106
They found residents in that valley and there were millions of them living in it.

503
00:40:20,746 --> 00:40:25,751
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام doesn't know that, this is the valley of ants, he was passing through it; his army was marching.

504
00:40:26,378 --> 00:40:28,718
حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَآ أَتَوْاْ عَلَىٰ وَادِ ٱلنَّمْلِ

505
00:40:29,378 --> 00:40:33,260
And when they came across the valley of ants.

506
00:40:34,500 --> 00:40:40,208
One of the ants saw the army approaching; it was the first and to see the army coming.

507
00:40:41,508 --> 00:40:44,258
What would be a natural reaction?

508
00:40:45,205 --> 00:40:54,895
When you see an army of humans, and Jinn(جِن), and birds in the air marching towards you, and you are the small creation; an insect,

509
00:40:55,268 --> 00:40:58,421
what would be the natural reaction in such a situation?

510
00:40:58,928 --> 00:41:03,241
To run; you would run; run away from danger.

511
00:41:05,408 --> 00:41:07,076
This was not the reaction of the ant.

512
00:41:07,523 --> 00:41:14,701
We would expect the natural reaction is that, you would immediately run away from this approaching danger.

513
00:41:14,947 --> 00:41:19,007
But the ant didn't do that, and Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! We find a lesson.

514
00:41:19,494 --> 00:41:23,306
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى doesn't mention anything in Qur'an except for a reason.

515
00:41:24,633 --> 00:41:30,426
We can have a whole talk about ants, and learn lessons from it,

516
00:41:30,959 --> 00:41:36,291
and find that we are lacking in things which this and it's kingdom had.

517
00:41:38,185 --> 00:41:44,218
This ants knew that if it runs away, it's not gonna survive.

518
00:41:45,485 --> 00:41:48,058
Because it's part of an ummah; it's part of a nation.

519
00:41:48,684 --> 00:41:52,451
And the survival of that ant depends on the survival of its ummah(امة).

520
00:41:53,491 --> 00:41:59,817
Because if the ummah(امة) is destroyed; it wouldn't do the ant any good even if it's alive; it's going to end up dying in the end.

521
00:42:00,563 --> 00:42:08,013
And this is something that every Muslim should learn and realize, that your survival is based on the survival of your ummah(امة).

522
00:42:09,313 --> 00:42:11,555
Never think that you can make it alone.

523
00:42:12,108 --> 00:42:18,677
You have to have the support of the ummah(امة), and you need to take care of the ummah(امة), and you need to be concerned about the ummah(امة).

524
00:42:18,864 --> 00:42:22,689
If you are not concerned about the ummah(امة), then realize that you're dead.

525
00:42:23,622 --> 00:42:32,320
If you do not have the concern that this ant had for its ummah(امة), then know that you are already dead before you even die.

526
00:42:32,693 --> 00:42:34,320
This ant said;

527
00:42:35,267 --> 00:42:38,949
يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّمْلُ ٱدْخُلُواْ مَسَٰكِنَكُمْ

528
00:42:39,209 --> 00:42:43,031
Oh you ants! Enter into your dwellings.

529
00:42:43,451 --> 00:42:44,811
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

530
00:42:45,144 --> 00:43:01,577
قَالَتْ نَمْلَةٌ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّمْلُ ٱدْخُلُواْ مَسَٰكِنَكُمْ لَا يَحْطِمَنَّكُمْ سُلَيْمَٰنُ وَجُنُودُهُۥ وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ۝

531
00:43:01,990 --> 00:43:05,632
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And one of the ants said;

532
00:43:05,912 --> 00:43:16,074
Oh ants! Enter your dwellings, lest Sulaiman(سليمان) and his hosts should crush you, while they perceive not.

533
00:43:16,988 --> 00:43:18,087
They might crush you.

534
00:43:19,987 --> 00:43:26,742
So it gave the advice to the whole ummah(امة) of ants, to go down in your dwellings.

535
00:43:27,709 --> 00:43:30,762
So it fulfilled its responsibility towards his ummah(امة).

536
00:43:33,395 --> 00:43:35,738
There's also something else we notice in the end of the Ayah(آية);

537
00:43:35,758 --> 00:43:36,711
وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ۝

538
00:43:36,731 --> 00:43:40,244
The ant said; that Sulaiman(سليمان) and his army would crush you.

539
00:43:40,264 --> 00:43:44,500
And what's worse than killing; I mean, the whole ummah(امة) of the ant could be dead.

540
00:43:44,693 --> 00:43:48,909
Nevertheless, the ant found an excuse for Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) and said;

541
00:43:48,929 --> 00:43:49,649
وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ۝

542
00:43:49,669 --> 00:43:51,702
And they don't proceed so; they don't know.

543
00:43:52,662 --> 00:43:55,933
It didn't say that, they're intentionally going to kill us and get rid of us; It said;

544
00:43:55,953 --> 00:43:56,786
وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ۝

545
00:43:56,973 --> 00:44:01,919
Even though, it's a matter of life and death; We are going to die; if we don't move from this place.

546
00:44:02,539 --> 00:44:07,424
Even though, we're going to lose our life; we're still going to give them an excuse.

547
00:44:08,044 --> 00:44:12,890
And we're going to say that, he's doing so; he doesn't intend to do so.

548
00:44:12,977 --> 00:44:14,003
وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ۝

549
00:44:14,630 --> 00:44:19,918
The ant is finding an excuse for Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) in something that has so importance, in the issue of life and death.

550
00:44:20,864 --> 00:44:25,908
Sometimes very minor things could happen between us, very minor things and we wouldn't find an excuse.

551
00:44:25,935 --> 00:44:31,664
In fact, we would try to indict a person, and to accuse a person.

552
00:44:31,977 --> 00:44:39,024
We, instead of trying to find 70 excuses for the person; we would try to find 70 ways to accuse a person.

553
00:44:39,519 --> 00:44:44,292
Over here, it's an issue of life and death, and the ant is still find an excuse for Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان), and saying;

554
00:44:44,485 --> 00:44:46,045
They don't perceive so; they don't know.

555
00:44:47,392 --> 00:44:52,217
These are important things that we can learn from An-Namlah(اَلنَّمْلَة); the ant.

556
00:44:54,184 --> 00:45:00,486
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام understands the language of the ants.

557
00:45:01,126 --> 00:45:02,859
And he heard what the ant said.

558
00:45:03,966 --> 00:45:06,015
فَتَبَسَّمَ ضَاحِكًا مِّن قَوْلِهَا

559
00:45:06,228 --> 00:45:07,215
So he smiled.

560
00:45:07,801 --> 00:45:13,931
When he heard this announcement from the ants; he smiled.

561
00:45:14,911 --> 00:45:19,556
So he; Solomon smiled; amused at her speech.

562
00:45:22,083 --> 00:45:29,868
This is a skill that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان); the ability to understand the language of the birds, and the ants.

563
00:45:32,008 --> 00:45:37,164
He attributed the credit and the thanks to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

564
00:45:38,430 --> 00:45:39,084
He said;

565
00:45:39,310 --> 00:45:43,317
قَالَ رَبِّ أَوْزِعْنِىٓ أَنْ أَشْكُرَ نِعْمَتَكَ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ

566
00:45:44,324 --> 00:45:50,451
Oh Allah! Gives me the ability to thank you and be grateful, for what you have given me.

567
00:45:51,964 --> 00:45:55,204
We; the ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ are the followers of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

568
00:45:56,124 --> 00:46:03,899
And we inherited all of the valid teachings of the prophets of Allah; in the form of the stories of Qur'an and the stories of Hadith(حديث).

569
00:46:04,952 --> 00:46:10,928
And all of the falsifications; that were attributed to the prophets and they are free from.

570
00:46:12,048 --> 00:46:21,054
Alhamdulillah(اَلْحَمْدُ لله)! In the religion of Islam; we, with the protection of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for the book of Islam; none of these crept in to the religion.

571
00:46:21,594 --> 00:46:23,398
So the valid teachings of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء);

572
00:46:23,418 --> 00:46:28,966
whether we're talking about Eesa(عيسى), or Musa(موسى), or Dawood(داؤد), or Sulaiman(سليمان), or Nuh(نوح), or Hud(هود), or Saleh(صالح);

573
00:46:29,320 --> 00:46:32,500
their teachings are given to us through Qur'an.

574
00:46:32,993 --> 00:46:35,297
And we follow the Sunan(سنن) of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

575
00:46:35,317 --> 00:46:40,176
We just talked about, for example; in Hajj(حَجْ); Rasool Allah ﷺ was standing in Hajj(حَجْ) and said;

576
00:46:40,256 --> 00:46:44,565
قِفوا على مشاعِرِكُم فإنَّكم على إرثٍ من إرثِ أبيكم إبراهيمَ

577
00:46:44,711 --> 00:46:46,805
Stand on your Masha'ir(مشاعِر).

578
00:46:46,838 --> 00:46:48,565
Masha'ir(مشاعِر) are the places of worship.

579
00:46:48,731 --> 00:46:53,890
Because you are on the inheritance of your father Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

580
00:46:54,070 --> 00:46:56,804
These are things we inherited from Sayidina Ibrahimعليه السلام.

581
00:46:57,464 --> 00:47:00,086
Over here, we find an important Sunnah(سنة).

582
00:47:01,579 --> 00:47:11,768
Whenever, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى blesses you with a skill; or blesses you with any Ni'mah(نعمة); whether it is wealth, or intelligence, or any ability.

583
00:47:12,335 --> 00:47:17,782
Whenever, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gives you this Ni'mah(نعمة); always thank Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for it.

584
00:47:18,575 --> 00:47:24,767
And whenever something good happens to you, due to that skill, then immediately follow it with Hamd(حَمد).

585
00:47:25,920 --> 00:47:31,765
For example; when you pass an exam; the first reaction should not be jumping up and down in happiness.

586
00:47:32,505 --> 00:47:34,745
Your first reaction should be Alhamdulillah(الحمدللہ)!

587
00:47:35,658 --> 00:47:42,753
If your business goes well; the first reaction should be not to say MashaAllah(ماشاالله); I'm a very intelligent and wise businessman.

588
00:47:43,513 --> 00:47:45,878
The first reaction which should be what?

589
00:47:46,018 --> 00:47:46,952
Alhamdulillah(اَلْحَمْدُ لله)!

590
00:47:47,412 --> 00:47:51,539
If Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you knowledge, and you are able to benefit someone with this knowledge,

591
00:47:51,659 --> 00:47:57,015
and you noticed that knowledge that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you, and you notice the fruits of that knowledge on somebody else,

592
00:47:57,415 --> 00:47:58,455
say; Alhamdulillah(اَلْحَمْدُ لله)!

593
00:47:58,801 --> 00:48:02,800
If Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you money and you have given away that money in the form of Sadaqah(صدقة).

594
00:48:02,987 --> 00:48:05,347
Immediately, after you give this Sadaqah(صدقة) say; Alhamdulillah(اَلْحَمْدُ لله)!

595
00:48:06,120 --> 00:48:12,362
Follow up every Ni'mah(نعمة) that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you with Shukr(شكر).

596
00:48:12,442 --> 00:48:17,808
That is the least that we could do to be grateful to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for what He has given us.

597
00:48:18,388 --> 00:48:38,135
فَتَبَسَّمَ ضَاحِكًا مِّن قَوْلِهَا وَقَالَ رَبِّ أَوْزِعْنِىٓ أَنْ أَشْكُرَ نِعْمَتَكَ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ وَعَلَىٰ وَٰللِدَىَّ وَأَنْ أَعْمَلَ صَٰلِحًا

598
00:48:39,375 --> 00:48:49,547
 وَأَنْ أَعْمَلَ صَٰلِحًا تَرْضَىٰهُ وَأَدْخِلْنِى بِرَحْمَتِكَ فِى عِبَادِكَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ۝

599
00:48:50,253 --> 00:48:52,087
He said; My Lord!

600
00:48:52,260 --> 00:49:04,159
Inspire me, and bestow upon me the power and ability, that I may be grateful for Your favours, which You have bestowed on me and on my parents,

601
00:49:04,551 --> 00:49:14,197
and that I may do righteous good deeds, that would please You and admit me by Your mercy among Your righteous slaves.

602
00:49:15,204 --> 00:49:17,259
A beautiful Dua(دُعَا) that we could remember.

603
00:49:17,892 --> 00:49:21,952
رَبِّ أَوْزِعْنِىٓ أَنْ أَشْكُرَ نِعْمَتَكَ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ وَعَلَىٰ  وَٰلِدَىَّ

604
00:49:22,265 --> 00:49:27,766
وَأَنْ أَعْمَلَ صَٰلِحًا تَرْضَىٰهُ وَأَأَدْخِلْنِى بِرَحْمَتِكَ فِى عِبَادِكَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ۝

605
00:49:28,846 --> 00:49:30,919
Let's go back to the Ayah(آية) we talked about earlier.

606
00:49:31,252 --> 00:49:37,834
وَحُشِرَ لِسُلَيْمَٰنَ جُنُودُهُۥ مِنَ ٱلْجِنِّ وَٱلْإِنسِ وَٱلطَّيْرِ فَهُمْ يُوزَعُونَ۝

607
00:49:38,288 --> 00:49:46,094
And the army of Sulaiman(سليمان) was assembled; the humans, the soldiers, the men, and the Jinn(جِن), and the birds; huge army.

608
00:49:46,541 --> 00:49:49,742
Keep this in mind and then let's look at the next Ayah(آية);

609
00:49:49,915 --> 00:50:00,617
وَتَفَقَّدَ الطَّيْرَ فَقَالَ مَا لِيَ لَا أَرَى الْهُدْهُدَ أَمْ كَانَ مِنَ اللْغَائِبِينَ۝

610
00:50:01,224 --> 00:50:04,008
He inspected the birds and said;

611
00:50:04,311 --> 00:50:10,523
What is the matter that I see not the hoopoe or is he among the absentees?

612
00:50:10,543 --> 00:50:13,103
Al-Hudhud(الهدهد) is a bird; hoopoe.

613
00:50:13,623 --> 00:50:14,537
We call it a bird.

614
00:50:16,670 --> 00:50:18,876
Sulaiman(سليمان) was inspecting his army.

615
00:50:19,869 --> 00:50:22,442
His army of thousands, or maybe millions.

616
00:50:22,682 --> 00:50:25,978
This huge army, which Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

617
00:50:26,025 --> 00:50:27,125
فَهُمْ يُوزَعُونَ۝

618
00:50:28,165 --> 00:50:31,019
And he noticed the absence of one bird.

619
00:50:31,779 --> 00:50:34,550
We find an important tip for leaders in this.

620
00:50:35,237 --> 00:50:36,770
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) was a king.

621
00:50:37,343 --> 00:50:39,409
He could spend his time in a palace.

622
00:50:40,369 --> 00:50:48,017
But he was there, in the battlefield, inspecting the army and he was able to notice the absence of one bird.

623
00:50:49,011 --> 00:50:50,051
One bird out of many.

624
00:50:50,451 --> 00:50:53,178
مَا لِيَ لَا أَرَى الْهُدْهُدَ أَمْ كَانَ مِنَ الْغَائِبِينَ۝

625
00:50:54,504 --> 00:51:01,990
So as I said; this might be a good tip or important lesson, for anybody who's in a position of leadership;

626
00:51:02,503 --> 00:51:07,313
to be able to realize their responsibility that they have towards their followers.

627
00:51:11,053 --> 00:51:14,539
He didn't find Al-Hudhud(الهدهد). So he said;

628
00:51:14,872 --> 00:51:29,185
لَأُعَذِّبَنَّهُۥ عَذَابًا شَدِيدًا أَوْ لَأَاْذْبَحَنَّهُۥٓ أَوْ لَيَأْتِيَنِّى بِسُلْطَٰنٍۢ مُّبِينٍۢ۝

629
00:51:29,665 --> 00:51:38,642
I will surely punish him with a severe torment, or even slaughter him, unless, he brings me a clear reason.

630
00:51:39,175 --> 00:51:42,769
The Hudhud(هدهد) was absent, Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said;

631
00:51:43,389 --> 00:51:44,322
Number one;

632
00:51:44,776 --> 00:51:52,679
I would punish him, a severe punishment, or slaughter him, if the sin is greater than I would slaughter him; the bird is dead,

633
00:51:53,299 --> 00:51:58,671
unless the bird presents me with a clear reason for being absent.

634
00:51:59,924 --> 00:52:02,131
You find here that the rule is very strict.

635
00:52:03,458 --> 00:52:05,622
Sulaiman(سليمان) didn't say I would let the bird go.

636
00:52:06,302 --> 00:52:07,982
It's either as punishment,

637
00:52:08,409 --> 00:52:08,915
and then he said;

638
00:52:08,935 --> 00:52:09,809
عَذَابًا شَدِيدًا

639
00:52:09,849 --> 00:52:12,197
It's not only punishment but severe.

640
00:52:12,997 --> 00:52:14,771
The second option is execution.

641
00:52:15,924 --> 00:52:16,991
أَوْ لَأَاْذْبَحَنَّهُۥ

642
00:52:17,357 --> 00:52:20,716
Unless, the bird brings me with a clear reason.

643
00:52:21,536 --> 00:52:24,864
The reason why the law over here is strict,

644
00:52:25,350 --> 00:52:27,749
is because; here we're dealing with what?

645
00:52:27,976 --> 00:52:31,256
We're dealing with a military situation; This is army.

646
00:52:32,516 --> 00:52:35,403
And if we look at the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

647
00:52:35,843 --> 00:52:41,358
we would find when Rasool Allah ﷺ is in the battlefield and going to Jihad(جهاد), the rules are strict.

648
00:52:41,478 --> 00:52:42,799
It's a military order.

649
00:52:43,679 --> 00:52:45,946
It's different than the rule in Madinah(مَدِينَه).

650
00:52:46,613 --> 00:52:47,862
I'll give you an example.

651
00:52:49,235 --> 00:52:51,602
In the Battle of Tabook(تبوك); Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

652
00:52:52,182 --> 00:52:54,210
لا يلحقن بنا الا مقوى

653
00:52:54,863 --> 00:52:58,650
Only one with strong transportation should follow us.

654
00:52:59,410 --> 00:53:04,835
Because the Battle of Tabook(تبوك); in that battle, they're going to be crossing the long deserts of Arabia.

655
00:53:04,882 --> 00:53:11,848
They're going to go all the way until the North passing Sahara An-Nufud(انّفود), which is a very rigid and tough environment and it's a long way.

656
00:53:12,088 --> 00:53:15,827
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Nobody should come with us unless their camel is strong.

657
00:53:16,260 --> 00:53:18,533
If your camel is weak, don't come.

658
00:53:19,687 --> 00:53:21,882
Because you're putting yourself in danger.

659
00:53:23,302 --> 00:53:29,371
One of the soldiers of the army really wanted to go out and fight in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

660
00:53:30,625 --> 00:53:35,073
he disobeyed the order and he came on a very weak camel.

661
00:53:35,340 --> 00:53:39,660
And he followed Rasool Allah ﷺ on that weak camel.

662
00:53:41,413 --> 00:53:46,029
Rasool Allah ﷺ has given clear orders; Don't come if you have a weak camel.

663
00:53:47,482 --> 00:53:50,071
That man disobeyed the order; What happened is;

664
00:53:50,325 --> 00:53:53,745
his camel fell down and the man died.

665
00:53:54,445 --> 00:53:58,776
Because the camel was weak; It couldn't withhold this difficult situation.

666
00:53:59,043 --> 00:54:03,436
So the camel fell down and this soldier fell off the camel and died.

667
00:54:04,470 --> 00:54:07,958
The Sahabahرضى الله عنهم were saying; Ash-Shaheed(اَلشَّهِيد) ! Ash-Shaheed(اَلشَّهِيد)!

668
00:54:08,312 --> 00:54:11,148
They said; Ash-Shaheed(اَلشَّهِيد); He became a Shaheed(شَهِيد); He died in the sake of Allah.

669
00:54:11,425 --> 00:54:16,267
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Don't say he's Shaheed(شَهِيد); he has disobeyed my orders.

670
00:54:18,034 --> 00:54:21,689
He is not a Shaheed(شَهِيد) because he disobeyed the order Rasool Allah ﷺ.

671
00:54:22,143 --> 00:54:31,515
Let's look at a similar situation in Madinah(مَدِينَه); the mother of Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) brought her son, Anas(أنس) to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

672
00:54:31,695 --> 00:54:34,544
I'm giving you away my son to be your servant.

673
00:54:35,957 --> 00:54:40,792
The Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ; they wanted to serve Rasool Allah ﷺ with their own life.

674
00:54:40,832 --> 00:54:42,952
They would give their lives for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

675
00:54:43,058 --> 00:54:47,427
This mother; she came and she brought her son Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) and said; Take my son to be your servant.

676
00:54:48,347 --> 00:54:50,194
So he would serve Rasool Allah ﷺ.

677
00:54:50,414 --> 00:54:55,966
One day, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; go out and buy me something, and he gave Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) some money.

678
00:54:56,986 --> 00:54:59,417
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) went to the market, he was still young.

679
00:54:59,904 --> 00:55:01,975
On the way he saw some children playing.

680
00:55:02,029 --> 00:55:08,222
So he took a turn and went to play with the kids and forgot about the order of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

681
00:55:09,142 --> 00:55:13,216
And time was dragging and he was playing.

682
00:55:13,463 --> 00:55:16,809
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ was waiting, Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) didn't come back;

683
00:55:16,849 --> 00:55:19,769
Rasool Allah ﷺ went out looking for him; he found him playing with the kids.

684
00:55:20,529 --> 00:55:21,757
He told him what happened?

685
00:55:21,923 --> 00:55:27,023
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) remembered the order of Rasool Allah ﷺ; he was checking his pockets, he found that he lost the money.

686
00:55:28,503 --> 00:55:32,473
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; continue playing, continue playing.

687
00:55:33,047 --> 00:55:35,073
Rasool Allah ﷺ forgive Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك).

688
00:55:35,233 --> 00:55:39,169
He lost the money; he didn't bring what Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to bring.

689
00:55:39,349 --> 00:55:41,409
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; continue to play.

690
00:55:43,116 --> 00:55:46,971
The more severe the situation; the stricter the rules are going to be.

691
00:55:48,058 --> 00:55:54,726
Because in a military situation, in an army; it is more severe situation so the rules are stricter.

692
00:55:55,353 --> 00:56:00,011
And we find that the Muslims lost in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) because of one rule that was broken.

693
00:56:00,805 --> 00:56:02,731
فَمَكَثَ غَيْرَ بَعِيدٍۢ

694
00:56:03,058 --> 00:56:05,310
But the hoopoe stayed not long.

695
00:56:05,817 --> 00:56:10,276
The hoopoe; the bird came back, and it came back with news.

696
00:56:10,882 --> 00:56:13,749
فَقَالَ أَحَطتُ بِمَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهِۦ

697
00:56:15,042 --> 00:56:19,751
I have grasped knowledge which you have not grasped.

698
00:56:20,305 --> 00:56:30,157
This bird is telling Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام, that I have grasped knowledge; I came over knowledge that you don't have.

699
00:56:31,163 --> 00:56:37,340
A statement like this, cannot be said to many kings in the world today; If you say that; you're dead.

700
00:56:37,727 --> 00:56:42,076
If you say that I have knowledge that you don't have; you could be dead.

701
00:56:43,109 --> 00:56:49,152
But Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام; a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; with the humbleness of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء);

702
00:56:50,065 --> 00:56:54,931
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) was willing to listen and to learn, even if it's coming from a bird.

703
00:56:56,044 --> 00:56:58,831
وَجِئْتُكَ مِن سَبَإٍ بِنَبَإٍۢ يَقِينٍ۝

704
00:56:59,938 --> 00:57:03,097
I have brought you from Saba'(سَبَإٍ); true news.

705
00:57:03,990 --> 00:57:11,809
Saba'(سَبَإٍ) is in Yemen, in an area called Ma'rib(معرب) that's the center or the capital of the Kingdom of Saba'(سَبَإٍ).

706
00:57:11,989 --> 00:57:17,938
And the Kingdom of Saba'(سَبَإٍ) was in a very fertile land and valley.

707
00:57:19,678 --> 00:57:21,946
But that area does not receive a lot of rain.

708
00:57:22,392 --> 00:57:28,012
The land is very fertile but the area does not receive a lot of rain.

709
00:57:28,037 --> 00:57:32,172
It only receives rain in two seasons and in very scarce amounts.

710
00:57:33,045 --> 00:57:35,821
Because the rain is received in two seasons.

711
00:57:36,861 --> 00:57:40,194
It is called in Arabic; Al-Antar Al-Mawsimiyyah(الانتار الموسميه).

712
00:57:41,167 --> 00:57:44,507
Mawsim(موسم) means, season; seasonal rain.

713
00:57:46,574 --> 00:57:55,119
The word Mawsim(موسم) was taken into English, and what is it called now; What do they call that type of rain?

714
00:57:55,239 --> 00:57:56,454
Monsoon rain.

715
00:57:56,787 --> 00:58:01,356
So the word monsoon comes from the Arabic word, Mawsim(موسم), which is seasonal rain.

716
00:58:03,663 --> 00:58:08,848
Because that area does not receive a lot of rain; the people of Saba'(سَبَإٍ) invented a dam.

717
00:58:09,135 --> 00:58:10,762
They built a dam in Ma'rib(معرب).

718
00:58:11,715 --> 00:58:16,484
And this dam was holding a lot of water that was coming down from the valleys and from the mountains,

719
00:58:16,878 --> 00:58:26,228
and they made an irrigation network that spread through areas, which are now in the Rub Al-Khali(ربع الخالى); in the empty quarter.

720
00:58:26,942 --> 00:58:30,091
And that was all gardens and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in Qur'an;

721
00:58:30,111 --> 00:58:34,607
لَقَدْ كَانَ لِسَبَإٍ فِي مَسْكَنِهِمْ آيَةٌ ۖ جَنَّتَانِ عَن يَمِينٍ وَشِمَالٍ ۖ

722
00:58:34,940 --> 00:58:36,014
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

723
00:58:36,034 --> 00:58:42,100
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given the people of Saba'(سَبَإٍ) in their land; an Ayah(آية); a sign, gardens from the right and left.

724
00:58:42,673 --> 00:58:47,393
Even though, the land is desert but because of that dam, it turn into gardens.

725
00:58:47,927 --> 00:58:52,132
This bird visited the kingdom of Saba'(سَبَإٍ).

726
00:58:52,212 --> 00:58:56,734
It went all the way from Jerusalem to Yemen; Pretty long distance.

727
00:58:57,921 --> 00:59:01,121
And it came back with news to Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

728
00:59:01,227 --> 00:59:02,206
The bird said;

729
00:59:02,839 --> 00:59:05,193
إِنِّي وَجَدتُّ امْرَأَةً تَمْلِكُهُمْ

730
00:59:06,059 --> 00:59:09,217
I found the woman ruling over them.

731
00:59:10,070 --> 00:59:14,550
And the name of this woman is; Al-Malika Bilqees(الملكه بلقيس); Her name is Bilqees(بلقيس).

732
00:59:16,443 --> 00:59:18,068
وَأُوتِيَتْ مِن كُلِّ شَيْءٍ

733
00:59:18,148 --> 00:59:20,174
And she was given from everything.

734
00:59:20,961 --> 00:59:27,470
Ibn Al-Jawzi(ابن الجوزى) says; This woman was given from everything that the king would want, or a queen would want.

735
00:59:28,170 --> 00:59:30,552
She had everything; wealth, power.

736
00:59:31,139 --> 00:59:32,632
وَلَهَا عَرْشٌ عَظِيمٌ۝

737
00:59:32,699 --> 00:59:33,986
And she has a great throne.

738
00:59:34,812 --> 00:59:37,724
Now Notice here that, the bird said; She has everything.

739
00:59:38,044 --> 00:59:40,271
But then the bird singled out her throne.

740
00:59:41,044 --> 00:59:41,504
Why?

741
00:59:41,524 --> 00:59:47,243
Because that throne was a sign for the kingdom of Saba'(سَبَإٍ).

742
00:59:47,463 --> 00:59:56,009
It was something that used to be a miracle of the world in its time; the throne of the queen of Saba'(سَبَإٍ).

743
00:59:56,675 --> 00:59:57,857
وَلَهَا عَرْشٌ عَظِيمٌ۝

744
00:59:57,911 --> 00:59:59,037
She has a great thrown.

745
01:00:01,191 --> 01:00:06,013
Up to this moment, it is praise of this huge and great civilization.

746
01:00:06,866 --> 01:00:08,040
أُوتِيَتْ مِن كُلِّ شَيْءٍ

747
01:00:08,080 --> 01:00:13,271
She has everything; she has a great throne; it's a huge kingdom.

748
01:00:15,657 --> 01:00:22,820
These are the standards that the people of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) use to classify nations.

749
01:00:23,934 --> 01:00:36,097
If the nation is rich, advanced, wealthy, we view that nation as civilized and advanced, and we try to imitate such nations.

750
01:00:37,017 --> 01:00:40,375
That is the standard that the people of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) have.

751
01:00:41,768 --> 01:00:43,455
But the bird was a Muslim.

752
01:00:44,108 --> 01:00:48,087
Even though, the bird said that, she has everything and she has a great throne.

753
01:00:48,474 --> 01:00:49,467
She said;

754
01:00:49,874 --> 01:00:54,100
وَجَدتُّهَا وَقَوْمَهَا يَسْجُدُونَ لِلشَّمْسِ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ

755
01:00:54,807 --> 01:01:00,059
I found her and her nation making Sujood(سجود) to the sun, instead of Allah.

756
01:01:00,679 --> 01:01:03,519
وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ

757
01:01:03,746 --> 01:01:07,544
And Satan has made their deeds fair seeming to them.

758
01:01:07,811 --> 01:01:11,584
فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ فَهُمْ لَا يَهْتَدُونَ۝

759
01:01:11,704 --> 01:01:15,116
And has barred them from Allah's way; so they have no guidance.

760
01:01:15,803 --> 01:01:23,589
The end result, of this surveillance of the bird is that; these are people who are misguided.

761
01:01:24,362 --> 01:01:35,199
The wealth, the power, the fact that they have everything, did not take the bird away from stating the fact that; this nation is a misguided nation.

762
01:01:35,892 --> 01:01:39,212
And this is the standard that we should view nations in.

763
01:01:40,066 --> 01:01:41,871
It is belief or Kuffr(كفر).

764
01:01:42,491 --> 01:01:44,704
It is either believing or non believing.

765
01:01:45,004 --> 01:01:47,404
And that is what counts on the day of judgment.

766
01:01:47,818 --> 01:01:53,483
And nation that could be heavy and strong in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), could be very light on the scale on the Day of Judgment.

767
01:01:53,890 --> 01:01:54,893
 And then the bird said;

768
01:01:54,967 --> 01:02:07,412
أَلَّا يَسْجُدُواْ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِى يُخْرِجُ ٱلْخَبْءَ فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُخْفُونَ وَمَا تُعْلِنُونَ۝

769
01:02:08,079 --> 01:02:16,421
Satan has barred them, so they do not worship Allah; Who brings to light what is hidden in the heavens and the earth,

770
01:02:16,621 --> 01:02:19,251
and knows what you conceal and what you reveal.

771
01:02:19,515 --> 01:02:22,776
ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ رَبُّ ٱلْعَرْشِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ۝

772
01:02:23,209 --> 01:02:30,447
The bird said; Allah! None has the right to be worshipped but He; The Lord of the supreme throne.

773
01:02:30,740 --> 01:02:37,526
Because, the bird in the beginning said that, she has a great throne; then the bird said; Allah is the One, Who Has a supreme throne.

774
01:02:38,740 --> 01:02:44,155
Even though, her throne is big but Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the One, Who Has the supreme throne.

775
01:02:44,342 --> 01:02:49,597
This is an Ayah(آية) of Sujood At-Tilawah(سجود تلاوة) so we will make Sujood(سجود).

776
01:02:49,764 --> 01:02:52,084
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام said;

777
01:02:52,297 --> 01:02:59,188
قَالَ سَنَنظُرُ أَصَدَقْتَ أَمْ كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ۝

778
01:02:59,701 --> 01:03:05,982
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام said; I will see if you are telling the truth or are you lying?

779
01:03:08,456 --> 01:03:10,221
So Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام said;

780
01:03:10,308 --> 01:03:12,774
سَنَنظُرُ أَصَدَقْتَ أَمْ كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ۝

781
01:03:12,881 --> 01:03:16,046
We will see, are you telling the truth or are you lying?

782
01:03:17,246 --> 01:03:27,848
ٱذْهَب بِّكِتَٰبِى هَٰذَا فَأَلْقِهْ إِلَيْهِمْ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَٱنظُرْ مَاذَا يَرْجِعُونَ۝

783
01:03:28,542 --> 01:03:35,911
Go you with this letter of mine and deliver it to them; then draw back from them and see; what answer they return.

784
01:03:36,571 --> 01:03:39,110
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام wrote a letter.

785
01:03:39,976 --> 01:03:46,883
And the Hudhud(هدهد) delivered this letter to the queen of Saba'(سَبَإٍ), in English; Sheba.

786
01:03:49,003 --> 01:03:50,129
Her name is Bilqees(بلقيس).

787
01:03:50,536 --> 01:03:57,553
So the Hudhud(هدهد) carried this letter and the story says that, the Hudhud(هدهد) delivered the letter on her lap.

788
01:03:58,840 --> 01:04:04,551
And then the Hudhud(هدهد) withdrew; so they didn't know where this letter came from.

789
01:04:04,571 --> 01:04:07,248
She just saw that this letter fell down on her lap.

790
01:04:08,221 --> 01:04:09,560
And Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said;

791
01:04:09,740 --> 01:04:11,300
فَٱنظُرْ مَاذَا يَرْجِعُونَ۝

792
01:04:11,333 --> 01:04:12,306
See what they're going to do.

793
01:04:12,506 --> 01:04:18,772
So the Hudhud(هدهد); even though, it withdrew from their sights, but it was monitoring their actions.

794
01:04:18,992 --> 01:04:24,415
The Hudhud(هدهد) was monitoring their actions to see; what their response will be.

795
01:04:24,801 --> 01:04:26,868
So the Queen opened the letter and she read it.

796
01:04:27,448 --> 01:04:31,556
The letter was very brief, and the contents were revealed to us in Qur'an.

797
01:04:32,543 --> 01:04:33,223
She said;

798
01:04:33,329 --> 01:04:45,146
قَالَتْ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْمَلَؤُاْ إِنِّىٓ أُلْقِىَ إِلَىَّ كِتَٰبٌ كَرِيمٌ۝

799
01:04:45,486 --> 01:04:51,584
She said: Oh chiefs! Verily, here is delivered to me a noble letter.

800
01:04:52,158 --> 01:04:53,038
كِتَٰبٌ كَرِيمٌ۝

801
01:04:53,078 --> 01:04:54,424
She said; The letter is noble.

802
01:04:54,998 --> 01:04:56,327
Why did she call it noble?

803
01:04:56,347 --> 01:04:57,111
Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ)!

804
01:04:57,384 --> 01:05:04,530
It could be because some of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) said; the way it looked, and the seal; it looked very noble.

805
01:05:04,910 --> 01:05:09,602
Some of them say; because of the contents of the letter which were noble.

806
01:05:10,215 --> 01:05:17,536
Some of them say; because of the source of the letter which is Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان); who is the noblest of his time.

807
01:05:19,116 --> 01:05:19,490
She said;

808
01:05:19,510 --> 01:05:21,163
أُلْقِىَ إِلَىَّ كِتَٰبٌ كَرِيمٌ۝

809
01:05:21,183 --> 01:05:24,095
A noble letter has been sent to me.

810
01:05:24,715 --> 01:05:25,589
Or actually,

811
01:05:25,935 --> 01:05:26,935
أُلْقِىَ إِلَىَّ

812
01:05:26,955 --> 01:05:29,213
Means; it fell on me.

813
01:05:30,062 --> 01:05:32,529
She doesn't even know who delivered it.

814
01:05:33,095 --> 01:05:35,681
And then she read the contents of this letter.

815
01:05:35,847 --> 01:05:39,781
It's very brief and listen to the contents.

816
01:05:41,027 --> 01:05:42,211
إِنَّهُۥ مِن سُلَيْمَٰنَ

817
01:05:42,534 --> 01:05:47,103
It is from Sulaiman(سليمان); That's the source; That's the one who's sending the letter.

818
01:05:48,536 --> 01:05:50,347
And keep in mind that Sulaiman(سليمان) is a king.

819
01:05:51,127 --> 01:05:52,974
He's a prophet; but he's also a king.

820
01:05:54,060 --> 01:05:55,767
And he's sending a letter to who?

821
01:05:56,227 --> 01:05:56,960
To a queen.

822
01:05:58,290 --> 01:06:06,778
If we don't know what the contents are, and we would be quizzed, to guess what the contents would be.

823
01:06:07,365 --> 01:06:11,513
I think it would be very difficult for us to reach to the right answer.

824
01:06:11,873 --> 01:06:20,212
If we're basing our opinion on the perception that we have, of what politics is, and how rulers, rule;

825
01:06:21,119 --> 01:06:30,133
we would assume that the letter would have contents which we hear regularly in the letters that are sent between kings and presidents all over the world.

826
01:06:31,160 --> 01:06:35,604
But if we are basing our opinion on the comprehensivity of Islam,

827
01:06:36,890 --> 01:06:44,573
and that Islam includes everything in life, and that the Shar'(شرء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى dominates everything that we do;

828
01:06:45,700 --> 01:06:49,825
then we would understand the contents of this letter.

829
01:06:50,965 --> 01:06:51,978
The letter is;

830
01:06:52,265 --> 01:07:01,827
إِنَّهُۥ مِن سُلَيْمَٰنَ وَإِنَّهُۥ بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ۝

831
01:07:02,080 --> 01:07:03,823
The letter starts with what?

832
01:07:04,116 --> 01:07:05,970
بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ۝

833
01:07:06,436 --> 01:07:09,715
We start our actions in the name of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

834
01:07:10,222 --> 01:07:12,728
We start eating by immensely the name of Allah.

835
01:07:12,908 --> 01:07:15,717
When we start As-Surah(السورة); we start by the name of Allah.

836
01:07:15,917 --> 01:07:20,923
When we ride our cars; we say; Bismillah(بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ); When we go on the airplane, we say Bismillah(بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ).

837
01:07:21,083 --> 01:07:24,735
Everything that we do, we should start it in the name of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

838
01:07:24,908 --> 01:07:27,855
And this is how, we would be following the Sunnah(سنة) of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

839
01:07:28,982 --> 01:07:31,004
إِنَّهُۥ بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ۝

840
01:07:31,204 --> 01:07:38,512
Verily, it is from Sulaiman(سليمان) and verily it reads In the Name of Allah; The Most Gracious, The Most Merciful.

841
01:07:39,505 --> 01:07:40,612
And then, what did he say?

842
01:07:40,978 --> 01:07:46,954
أَلَّا تَعْلُواْ عَلَىَّ وَأْتُونِى مُسْلِمِينَ۝

843
01:07:47,234 --> 01:07:55,286
He said; Be you not exalted against me, but come to me as Muslims; submit to me.

844
01:07:55,606 --> 01:07:56,766
And that's the end of the letter.

845
01:07:57,406 --> 01:07:58,982
أَلَّا تَعْلُواْ عَلَىَّ

846
01:07:59,462 --> 01:08:01,482
Don't be exalted over me.

847
01:08:01,982 --> 01:08:07,998
Don't view yourself in a better position, or in a higher position, or in a position of arrogance.

848
01:08:09,405 --> 01:08:14,178
And Sulaiman(سليمان) is not saying that to satisfy a personal desire;

849
01:08:14,812 --> 01:08:18,072
but he's saying that because he's the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

850
01:08:18,092 --> 01:08:19,165
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

851
01:08:19,185 --> 01:08:22,630
وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَا مِن رَّسُولٍ إِلَّا لِيُطَاعَ بِإِذْنِ ٱللَّهِ ۚ

852
01:08:23,110 --> 01:08:26,710
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; We have sent every messenger to be obeyed.

853
01:08:27,577 --> 01:08:29,136
The messengers; we obey them.

854
01:08:29,416 --> 01:08:33,963
They are the ones who are in the high level, and they are the ones who issued orders to us.

855
01:08:34,456 --> 01:08:43,024
So he is telling her don't think that since you are in the same political rank; I'm the king and you're the queen, that we are on the same level.

856
01:08:43,644 --> 01:08:45,478
I am the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

857
01:08:45,498 --> 01:08:48,691
you don't see me as a king; Now, see me as the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

858
01:08:48,805 --> 01:08:49,651
أَلَّا تَعْلُواْ عَلَىَّ

859
01:08:49,671 --> 01:08:50,911
Don't be exalted against me.

860
01:08:51,245 --> 01:08:52,398
وَأْتُونِى مُسْلِمِينَ۝

861
01:08:52,418 --> 01:08:53,424
And come to me;

862
01:08:53,650 --> 01:09:00,559
it is translated here as Muslims, but many of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) say; it means, submission; come to me in the form of submission.

863
01:09:01,186 --> 01:09:03,213
Submit to me and then, he's going to give them Da'wah(دعوة).

864
01:09:03,666 --> 01:09:08,662
So over here Muslimeen(مُسْلِمِينَ) does not mean the religion; come to me as Muslims.

865
01:09:08,682 --> 01:09:10,868
It means; come to me in the form of submission.

866
01:09:11,108 --> 01:09:12,788
Because that's what Islam means.

867
01:09:13,615 --> 01:09:14,648
وَأْتُونِى مُسْلِمِينَ۝

868
01:09:14,673 --> 01:09:18,688
It means submit to my orders and commands to you.

869
01:09:20,082 --> 01:09:24,434
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تسلیما کثیرا

